    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 all tests pass, including the new `coreComputesInitials` acceptance test expecting `J.S.`.\n\nSummary of the change:\n\n- **`Person.java`** (`model`): added a derived `getInitials()` method \u2014 the single owner of this logic \u2014 returning the upper-cased first letters of `firstName`/`lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (`\"J.S.\"`). Marked `@Transient` so JPA doesn't treat it as a persistent column. Since it lives on `Person`, it's automatically available to any `Person` subclass (e.g. `Vet`).\n- **`openapi.yml`**: added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field in the JSON response.\n\nMapStruct then auto-maps `ownerDto.setInitials(owner.getInitials())` in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl` \u2014 no mapper code needed, mirroring how the existing `displayName` reads from the domain object. No logic was duplicated.",
